    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xzyb1tn",
      "content": "Pharmacology is the science that studies drugs, their sources, properties, actions, therapeutic uses, side effects, and mechanisms of action in the human body. For nursing competitive examinations such as RRB Nursing, pharmacology is one of the most important subjects. Questions are commonly asked from drug classifications, routes of administration, pharmacokinetics, pharmacodynamics, antibiotics, analgesics, cardiovascular drugs, endocrine drugs, and emergency medications."
    },
    {
